Description: UAC live response - processes, network, open files and kernel modules at collection time
Category: LiveResponse
Author: ArtefactForge
Version: '1.0'
ExportFormat: csv
OutputName: LinuxLiveResponse
# What UAC's live_response commands recorded about the running system: the process list with each
# process's executable, working directory and hashes from /proc; sockets with their owning
# processes (ss, else netstat); interface addresses, routes and the neighbour cache; lsof's open
# files with deleted-but-open ones marked; and loaded kernel modules with their taint flags.
# Processes get a Review column (deleted executable, running from /tmp or /dev/shm or memory, a
# shell or download one-liner), and a process /proc listed but ps did not is added and marked.
#
# Every file under live_response is listed in LinuxLiveResponse_Index.csv with the CSV that read
# it, so command output not parsed here (iptables, systemctl, env, sestatus and the rest) is still
# in view. ps times are the collected system's local time, written as recorded.
#
# Reads %root%\_UAC\live_response, where a UAC collection's command output lands on extraction.
Requires:
  - '%root%/_UAC/live_response'
Platform: linux
Priority: 8
IoWeight: light
Processors:
  -
    Executable: builtin:LinuxLiveResponse
    CommandLine: --root "%root%" --out "%destinationDirectory%"
    ExportFormat: csv
